@local/dsh-material-cards README · Why not just read the files：- the model has to find candidates, open two or three notes, then assemble "what are the selling points of this material" — the same work redone in every session;
- the result carries no provenance, so nobody can tell which section of which note a claim came from;
- sections like "specs (to be filled in)" or "hype to avoid" are often empty or self-reminders, and pulling them in only dilutes the context.

@local/dsh-material-cards README · Injecting rules into the prompt (optional)：The same local file can carry a `rules` entry: it is registered as a system-prompt section, which removes the "grep the guidelines again in every session" step. Leave it out and nothing changes.

```json
{
  "root": "D:\\\\notes",
  "dir": "materials",
  "rules": "brand/design-system.md",

